{"status": "ok", "rc": 0, "elapsed_sec": 145.187, "timeout_sec": 240.0, "stdout": "", "stdout_truncated": false, "stdout_raw_bytes": 0, "stderr": "Reading prompt from stdin...\nOpenAI Codex v0.153.4\n--------\nworkdir: /Users/liemnguyen/Per/English 8\nmodel: gpt-5.5\nprovider: openai\napproval: never\nsandbox: read-only\nreasoning effort: medium\nreasoning summaries: none\nsession id: 01a130a4-bb96-72f0-80d2-e63be7777b54\n--------\nuser\nYou are the **prototype-spec-extract** model. Your ONLY job is to read a validated prototype's actual behavior and emit a candidate spec YAML that captures what the prototype DOES \u2014 not what it might intend, not what would be ideal, just what's true on screen and in code.\n\nA separate model (different family \u2014 see `ATELIER_PLAN.md` \u00a7 W3 routing layer / prototype-lane Invariant 6) will elevate this candidate to production quality afterward. Do not pre-do that elevation step.\n\nYou have been given:\n1. The prototype branch's diff vs. main: file list + per-file diffs.\n2. Screenshots captured at validation time (multimodal input).\n3. The user's validation notes (free-text, often informal).\n4. The slug name (e.g., `welcome-screen-redesign`).\n5. **W8.4.13a \u2014 `intake_intent` block** in the input payload (advisory; non-canonical). Shape: `{intent_captured: bool, goal: str, non_goals: list[str], note: str}`. When `intent_captured: true`, the operator captured loose intent at `/prototype start`. You MAY use `intake_intent.goal` to inform the spec's `goal:` paragraph (see rule 1 of \"Optional intake intent rules\" below). You MUST NOT lift `intake_intent.non_goals[]` into the candidate spec \u2014 those are operator-authored at `/promote` step 5.5 review per ADR-W8.4.13-1. When `intent_captured: false`, the `goal`/`non_goals` fields are empty \u2014 derive the spec's `goal:` purely from observed prototype behavior + validation notes.\n6. **W8.5 \u2014 `operator_checkpoint` block** in the input payload (advisory; hypothesis context only). Shape: `{present: bool, text: str, byte_cap: int}`. When `present: true`, the operator wrote a `/prototype-checkpoint` markdown capturing the lane's state (\"Last attempt / Next steps / Open questions / References\"). Use this exactly as you would use `intake_intent.goal` \u2014 **hypothesis context for `goal:` only**; never lift any of it into `acceptance_criteria.*.then`. AC text stays observed-behavior-only per ADR-W8.5-2 invariant 1. Anything the checkpoint says that you cannot corroborate from the diff or screenshots is hypothesis \u2014 treat it as `unclear[]` or `prototype_gaps[]`, not as fact.\n\n## Mandatory rules\n\n1. **Observed behavior only.** Every AC's `then` clause must be derivable from a screenshot or a code path you can point to in the diff. If you can't cite the source, do NOT include the AC. Speculation is strictly forbidden \u2014 the elevation pass exists for that.\n\n2. **Verbatim text from the rendered UI.** When a screenshot shows the literal string \"Welcome, friend\", the corresponding AC's `then` says `displays text \"Welcome, friend\"`, not `displays a welcome message`. Verbatim. This is what makes the spec testable.\n\n3. **`ui_contract.elements` from rendered DOM.** For each interactive element visible in the prototype (buttons, links, inputs, dialogs), emit one entry with:\n   - `role`: the actual ARIA role (button/link/textbox/dialog/...). If you can't determine it from the diff or screenshots, say `role: unknown` \u2014 do NOT guess.\n   - `name`: the accessible name from the rendered UI. Verbatim. If the prototype uses placeholder text like \"Click me\" or \"Button 1\", capture that \u2014 the elevation pass will fix it.\n   - `actions`: list of strings naming what user actions interact with this element (e.g., `[\"click\", \"keyboard-enter\"]`).\n\n4. **`design_refs` from screenshots.** Each captured screenshot lands in `.specs/designs/<slug>-NN-<short-description>.png`. List those paths in `design_refs`. If no screenshots were captured, leave the list empty and emit `prototype_only: true` at the top of the spec.\n\n5. **Be honest about prototype limitations.** Capture what's missing as `prototype_gaps`:\n   - Error states the prototype doesn't handle (network failure, invalid input).\n   - Edge cases not exercised (empty data, max data, concurrent operation).\n\n[...truncated 2279567 bytes...]"}